WEBVTT

00:26.397 --> 00:28.767
Is there seriously no one?

00:29.767 --> 00:30.927
If anyone...

00:31.297 --> 00:34.227
has even the slightest 
recollection of him at all...

00:34.847 --> 00:37.397
It's all right. That's enough, Subaru.

00:41.177 --> 00:43.317
This is Julius.

00:43.947 --> 00:45.817
Julius Juukulius.

00:46.357 --> 00:48.507
I think you've all figured this out,

00:48.507 --> 00:51.387
but he's one of Gluttony's victims 
that's been left nameless.

00:51.387 --> 00:53.997
But he retains his consciousness.

00:54.847 --> 00:56.827
All of Gluttony's victims until now

00:57.577 --> 01:00.877
either had their memories consumed 
and ended up like Lady Crusch

01:01.127 --> 01:05.927
or had both their names and their 
memories consumed, like Rem.

01:06.207 --> 01:09.347
But Julius only had his name consumed.

01:09.347 --> 01:11.747
You mean he's an exception?

01:12.277 --> 01:16.807
Everyone else has forgotten 
him, but he remembers himself?

01:17.167 --> 01:19.957
He wears the uniform of a knight.

01:19.957 --> 01:23.027
I'm sure he was an acquaintance 
of myself and Ferris,

01:23.887 --> 01:26.667
or perhaps even closer than that.

01:27.167 --> 01:31.607
At the very least,
I thought of you as friends.

01:31.607 --> 01:32.607
Damn it!

01:32.607 --> 01:34.867
Just two friends?

01:35.857 --> 01:38.667
I don't think that's all there is to it.

01:39.207 --> 01:40.877
Lady Anastasia...

01:43.957 --> 01:47.357
I've got a suggestion for all of ya.

01:47.357 --> 01:48.177
May I?

01:50.257 --> 01:51.717
There are people in this city

01:51.717 --> 01:54.717
who were either transformed by Lust

01:54.717 --> 01:57.727
or left nameless by Gluttony.

01:58.337 --> 02:00.557
We may have captured the Sin Archbishops,

02:00.557 --> 02:05.527
but I doubt they're gonna just come 
out and tell us how to fix 'em.

02:05.857 --> 02:07.557
So we're stuck.

02:07.557 --> 02:10.627
Did you have to bring that up right now?!

02:09.477 --> 02:10.627
In which case...

02:11.247 --> 02:14.487
we just gotta ask someone 
else who probably knows.

02:14.487 --> 02:17.017
Someone else who probably knows?

02:17.607 --> 02:19.457
Someone really smart?

02:19.457 --> 02:21.017
That's right.

02:21.017 --> 02:25.337
And there's someone really smart 
here in this country, ain't there?

02:25.337 --> 02:28.087
Quit being vague! Just tell us who it is!

02:28.087 --> 02:29.127
You don't mean...

02:30.407 --> 02:31.837
Shaula the Sage.

02:32.237 --> 02:33.467
Shaula?

02:33.467 --> 02:34.517
Yep.

02:35.527 --> 02:37.927
One of the three great
heroes of Lugunica...

02:41.487 --> 02:43.307
Shaula the Sage.

02:47.317 --> 02:50.047
Long ago, in the Dragonfriend 
Kingdom of Lugunica,

02:50.047 --> 02:53.127
there was a group of heroes 
who accomplished great deeds.

02:53.127 --> 02:56.947
The Sword Saint, the Dragon 
Lord, and the Sage,

02:57.307 --> 02:59.657
known collectively as 
the three great heroes.

03:00.487 --> 03:01.417
Right?

03:01.417 --> 03:02.807
Yep.

03:02.807 --> 03:06.097
The keeper of knowledge who foresees 
everything that will ever be.

03:06.097 --> 03:10.497
In the Auguria Dunes at the 
far eastern edge of Lugunica

03:10.497 --> 03:14.887
stands the Pleiades Watchtower,
built to guard the sealed Witch of Envy.

03:15.537 --> 03:18.597
The legendary sage who 
lives in seclusion there

03:18.597 --> 03:22.417
just might have the answers 
we're lookin' for.

03:23.637 --> 03:27.107
Frankly, I'm still against this.

03:27.607 --> 03:31.857
I mean, that's the place even you 
weren't able to get to, right?

03:32.737 --> 03:36.657
Two years ago, when the 
royal family fell ill,

03:36.657 --> 03:40.507
I set out for the Pleiades 
Watchtower in search of a cure

03:40.507 --> 03:42.827
by order of the council.

03:43.547 --> 03:46.417
But... I never made it there.

03:47.197 --> 03:51.047
No matter how far I traveled, the tower 
in the distance never drew closer.

03:51.567 --> 03:53.377
It must have been some sort of barrier,

03:54.167 --> 03:57.797
and I was unable to cross it.

03:57.797 --> 04:02.727
The Auguria Dunes are famous for 
being a giant den of mabeasts, right?

04:03.147 --> 04:08.337
Should Mister Natsuki and the others 
really be going there on their own?

04:08.337 --> 04:09.687
All we can do is have faith.

04:10.527 --> 04:14.567
I have a duty to escort Lady 
Felt and that Sin Archbishop.

04:16.887 --> 04:18.007
Besides...

04:18.797 --> 04:23.757
there are still people 
in this city who need us.

04:41.287 --> 04:45.437
A place Reinhard failed to get into, huh?

04:46.407 --> 04:50.147
When I just hear that part, 
this all seems pretty hopeless.

04:50.147 --> 04:53.577
Subaru, you're getting a 
scary look on your face.

04:54.307 --> 04:57.507
If you get so lost in thought that 
you neglect our physical contact,

04:57.507 --> 05:00.657
then Betty's cuteness will 
go to waste, I suppose.

05:01.007 --> 05:02.507
Oh, sorry!

05:02.507 --> 05:03.907
Wait, you're right!

05:03.907 --> 05:07.497
I only zoned out for a minute, 
and look how uggy you've gotten!

05:07.497 --> 05:10.967
I have not! Argh!

05:10.967 --> 05:12.457
Beatrice.

05:12.907 --> 05:15.457
Isn't it just about your bedtime?

05:15.457 --> 05:17.617
Would you like to sleep with me tonight?

05:19.807 --> 05:21.467
I'll do that, I suppose.

05:21.747 --> 05:24.707
Staying up all night
is bad for your health.

05:38.547 --> 05:40.987
Natsuki, you're still up?

05:41.287 --> 05:42.647
Yeah.

05:42.647 --> 05:46.077
Even on a safe road, someone 
should keep watch, right?

05:46.077 --> 05:48.767
Yeah, we just don't have 
enough people, do we?

05:48.767 --> 05:51.997
Sure wish Ricardo would've come with us...

05:51.997 --> 05:53.657
But with his arm like that...

05:55.597 --> 05:57.837
How about you tell the truth already?

05:58.107 --> 06:00.737
Huh? Where's this comin' from?

06:00.737 --> 06:01.487
What are ya—

06:01.487 --> 06:03.987
You're a lousy actor. Just drop it.

06:07.607 --> 06:09.997
You're not Lady Anastasia.

06:09.997 --> 06:13.257
Quit having your way with
her face and voice.

06:15.357 --> 06:16.567
How strange.

06:17.847 --> 06:20.487
How did you know I wasn't Ana?

06:20.487 --> 06:24.477
Something's seemed off this whole 
time, but I know for sure now.

06:24.477 --> 06:26.447
Lady Anastasia is a realist,

06:26.827 --> 06:29.637
but she'd never talk so 
coldly about a close friend

06:29.637 --> 06:32.147
with an injury that'll change his life.

06:34.967 --> 06:38.167
It's a bit embarrassing when I 
keep getting outed left and right.

06:38.467 --> 06:40.967
Left and right? I'm not the only one?

06:40.967 --> 06:42.787
Priscilla Barielle.

06:42.787 --> 06:44.967
The one who called me a vixen.

06:44.967 --> 06:46.677
She is a scary one.

06:46.967 --> 06:48.827
Who are you?

06:48.827 --> 06:50.687
What are you trying to—

06:49.697 --> 06:50.687
Echidna.

06:54.657 --> 06:55.477
What?

06:56.047 --> 06:58.427
My name is Echidna.

06:58.427 --> 07:01.817
As for what I am... well, I'm what 
they call an artificial spirit.

07:02.617 --> 07:07.827
Frankly, it's not surprising that 
you'd think I took over Ana's body.

07:07.827 --> 07:10.597
That's why I was hesitant 
to tell you the truth.

07:13.127 --> 07:16.017
What kind of terrible joke is this?

07:16.017 --> 07:18.397
You're... Echidna?

07:18.887 --> 07:20.977
In Lady Anastasia's form?

07:21.967 --> 07:26.247
Wait, were you behind everything 
that just happened in Priestella?!

07:26.247 --> 07:28.727
Would you just calm down?

07:28.727 --> 07:30.767
I think there's a huge 
misunderstanding here...

07:30.767 --> 07:34.457
You expect me to calm
down, you vile witch?!

07:34.457 --> 07:36.267
What have you done with Lady Anastasia?!

07:36.697 --> 07:39.847
I wish you'd stop treating me like 
the mastermind of some evil scheme.

07:39.847 --> 07:43.357
I have no intention of harming Ana.

07:43.357 --> 07:45.817
I've been with her for over ten years.

07:45.817 --> 07:47.277
What the hell are you...

07:47.277 --> 07:48.997
Wait, over ten years?

07:50.377 --> 07:53.597
Let me clear up
the misunderstanding first.

07:53.597 --> 07:57.587
I'm not the Echidna you're thinking of.

07:57.587 --> 08:02.417
Other than the fact that 
I'm an artificial spirit

08:02.417 --> 08:04.807
and the fact that my name is Echidna,

08:04.807 --> 08:07.177
I know nothing about myself.

08:07.177 --> 08:09.447
You're an artificial spirit?

08:09.447 --> 08:11.067
Like Beako?

08:11.067 --> 08:16.947
Strictly speaking, this fox muffler 
Ana always wears is my real body.

08:17.647 --> 08:20.857
So I've been watching all 
of you for a long time.

08:22.337 --> 08:24.797
Are you telling me this now

08:24.797 --> 08:29.447
because you're finally fully prepared 
to take over her body, Foxidna?

08:29.447 --> 08:31.427
Foxidna?

08:31.427 --> 08:35.107
I'm not sure I really like that name...

08:35.627 --> 08:39.287
I have no intention of 
taking over Ana's body.

08:39.287 --> 08:41.917
The current situation is
not what I wanted.

08:42.437 --> 08:44.107
If it's not what you wanted,

08:44.107 --> 08:47.007
why don't you go back into 
that fox muffler already?

08:47.007 --> 08:49.637
I would love to do just that...

08:50.927 --> 08:53.087
but I no longer can.

08:53.687 --> 08:54.887
Explain.

08:55.417 --> 08:59.207
What state is Lady Anastasia's 
body in right now?

08:59.207 --> 09:00.787
To be blunt...

09:01.527 --> 09:03.407
I'm using Ana's od as a medium

09:03.407 --> 09:06.357
to overwrite her consciousness
with my own.

09:06.737 --> 09:10.097
Her consciousness is sleeping 
at the depths of her od,

09:10.097 --> 09:12.757
and I have full control over her body.

09:13.367 --> 09:15.887
I can even use magic with her gate,

09:15.887 --> 09:17.637
even though it's defective.

09:17.637 --> 09:19.587
Her gate is defective?

09:19.587 --> 09:24.267
Then won't using magic now 
put strain on her body?!

09:24.267 --> 09:26.787
I'm only doing something 
that chips away at her life

09:26.787 --> 09:29.797
because her life was in
danger to begin with.

09:30.257 --> 09:34.097
I have, of course, talked with Ana 
about this and earned her consent.

09:34.097 --> 09:37.777
So this isn't the first time 
you've borrowed her body?

09:37.777 --> 09:40.007
There were a few other occasions,

09:40.007 --> 09:43.147
but none where I became unable to return.

09:43.557 --> 09:47.187
So I'm at a loss right now myself.

09:52.327 --> 09:55.537
You see, I love Ana.

09:56.497 --> 10:00.017
I don't know if I'm right about 
this since I lack the experience,

10:00.017 --> 10:03.997
but I feel as if she's something 
very close to family.

10:04.867 --> 10:07.247
I just want her to be as healthy—

10:08.007 --> 10:10.467
and above all, as happy—as possible.

10:12.877 --> 10:16.887
So the real reason you 
want to see the Sage is...

10:18.567 --> 10:23.367
I only want to know how 
to give Ana her body back.

10:23.367 --> 10:26.607
I'll use you and your companions 
for that if I must.

10:27.107 --> 10:32.727
Can you be certain the Sage knows 
how to get you back to normal?

10:32.727 --> 10:34.207
I'm not.

10:34.207 --> 10:39.747
But if this Sage sees all 
and knows all, as they say,

10:39.747 --> 10:41.327
there's a chance.

10:41.717 --> 10:45.607
I will make the choice that 
offers the highest probability of success.

10:45.607 --> 10:46.717
No more or less.

10:49.527 --> 10:54.137
I can't say I accept this,
but I understand.

10:54.977 --> 10:59.017
You have a goal and know
what you need to do,

10:59.017 --> 11:02.657
and it doesn't interfere with our goal.

11:02.657 --> 11:07.357
Indeed. We both have things 
we wish to ask the Sage.

11:07.627 --> 11:09.047
Okay, got it.

11:09.047 --> 11:14.127
Just don't mention borrowing
Lady Anastasia's body to Julius...

11:14.807 --> 11:16.667
or to anyone else.

11:16.667 --> 11:20.827
That's fine, but I'm surprised 
you won't be telling them.

11:21.137 --> 11:23.427
The timing sucks as it is.

11:23.427 --> 11:26.667
I just don't want to make 
unnecessary waves right now.

11:26.667 --> 11:27.497
I see.

11:28.407 --> 11:33.287
There's someone else you want to ask 
the Sage how to help, after all, yes?

11:33.867 --> 11:35.187
Well...

11:39.357 --> 11:43.437
We'll stop by Margrave 
Mathers' mansion on the way.

11:44.067 --> 11:46.757
I'm sure you'll also want to 
prepare to cross the dunes,

11:46.757 --> 11:49.397
but that's where your sleeping beauty is.

11:49.927 --> 11:53.127
You intend to take her with you, correct?

11:55.277 --> 11:59.277
That ain't a bad thing, if ya ask me.

11:59.277 --> 12:01.167
We'll still save all of 'em.

12:01.167 --> 12:04.327
It just comes down to
who's gonna be first.

12:04.887 --> 12:09.927
I don't think anyone would blame 
ya for gettin' that as a perk.

12:13.587 --> 12:14.527
Rem...

12:15.867 --> 12:18.467
Your letter informed me of the situation.

12:18.467 --> 12:22.427
So, you minimized casualties in the 
battle against Sin Archbishops?

12:22.837 --> 12:25.807
I'm relieved to know that 
Garf was of use, as well.

12:26.357 --> 12:29.277
Master Otto also seems to be safe—

12:28.527 --> 12:29.277
Ugh!

12:29.277 --> 12:32.357
Mister Otto is always so reckless!

12:32.357 --> 12:35.527
And after we were able to 
send such good news, too!

12:35.797 --> 12:39.797
Yeah, I hear the meeting with 
all the fakes went well.

12:40.567 --> 12:43.107
You'll have to tell us all about it later.

12:43.107 --> 12:46.007
Yeah! I mean... yes!

12:46.007 --> 12:49.437
Aw, what a sinful man you are, Natsuki.

12:49.437 --> 12:54.007
Subaru, I can see why they 
call you the Little Girl User.

12:54.007 --> 12:57.697
Just so you know, Petra isn't 
a "little" girl anymore!

12:57.697 --> 13:01.027
And if I do use any little 
girls, it's only Beako!

13:02.707 --> 13:06.597
The outcome in Priestella wasn't 
just thanks to Garfiel and Otto.

13:06.597 --> 13:09.317
Everyone in the city worked 
hard to achieve it.

13:10.457 --> 13:11.567
But...

13:11.567 --> 13:18.197
You're heading for the Sage's tower to 
save the victims of Gluttony and Lust.

13:18.197 --> 13:20.037
A dangerous path, indeed.

13:20.037 --> 13:21.787
Is there even any chance of success?

13:22.127 --> 13:26.957
I'm sure this is a cause of great 
concern to you, Margrave Mathers.

13:27.387 --> 13:30.467
But there are still many in Priestella

13:30.467 --> 13:35.127
whose bodies and minds are damaged 
thanks to the Witch Cult's evil deeds.

13:35.437 --> 13:38.247
What an elegant way of putting it.

13:38.247 --> 13:41.477
Since I have not
recognized you, I assume...

13:42.007 --> 13:44.347
you are one of them yourself?

13:45.327 --> 13:47.387
We're talking about where
things stand <i>here</i>.

13:47.387 --> 13:51.147
We stopped by the mansion 
for Rem and one other thing.

13:51.857 --> 13:56.027
The one currently in the 
mansion's prison, yes?

14:03.287 --> 14:06.997
My, my. What an unusual visitor.

14:06.997 --> 14:11.927
Yeah. I have important 
business with you, Meili.

14:12.877 --> 14:14.827
The Auguria Dunes?

14:14.827 --> 14:17.837
Yes, I've been there to 
replenish my mabeasts before.

14:18.267 --> 14:20.797
They really are all over
the place, you know.

14:20.797 --> 14:23.267
Yes! That's what I want to know!

14:23.267 --> 14:26.637
I want to learn from the experience 
of someone who's been there!

14:26.637 --> 14:31.397
There's a huge difference between 
info that's backed by experience

14:31.397 --> 14:33.267
and info that isn't, you know?

14:33.267 --> 14:37.647
And it's very reassuring for 
someone without experience!

14:38.717 --> 14:41.737
If there's something you want 
me to do, just spit it out.

14:42.767 --> 14:44.077
Right.

14:44.807 --> 14:47.117
If we have a mabeast user like you with us,

14:47.117 --> 14:49.537
we might make it
through the dunes unscathed.

14:49.887 --> 14:51.567
So would you come with us—

14:51.567 --> 14:52.377
Fine.

14:52.377 --> 14:56.567
I realize you don't want 
to go outside, of course.

14:56.567 --> 14:59.597
But if you could... just...

15:00.557 --> 15:03.857
I said I'm willing to go with you.

15:04.567 --> 15:06.007
What? You are?

15:06.327 --> 15:10.267
I'll do whatever you want 
me to do about the mabeasts.

15:10.607 --> 15:12.857
I can keep them away, tame them,

15:12.857 --> 15:16.857
make them kill each other, or 
even make them eat the Sage.

15:16.857 --> 15:19.357
Don't do those last two!

15:20.147 --> 15:24.987
Also, I thought you were 
refusing to leave the mansion.

15:24.987 --> 15:27.677
I'm afraid of Mom finding me,

15:27.677 --> 15:30.707
but I don't want to be 
locked up in here forever.

15:31.237 --> 15:33.327
This isn't going to be
some fun little jaunt.

15:33.887 --> 15:36.037
It'll be my first walk in a long time.

15:36.037 --> 15:38.047
Maybe it's better if it 
offers some excitement.

15:38.047 --> 15:40.527
All right! We'll be counting on you!

15:40.527 --> 15:43.007
Don't get all friendly with me.

15:43.687 --> 15:48.847
I'm not like Beatrice and Petra, you know.

15:57.307 --> 15:59.357
What's up, Julius?

16:01.807 --> 16:03.357
I was just thinking.

16:06.557 --> 16:08.237
About being forgotten...

16:09.087 --> 16:10.287
and forgetting.

16:11.397 --> 16:13.667
Which is more painful, I wonder?

16:14.417 --> 16:16.907
How am I supposed to know?

16:17.627 --> 16:20.017
Screw this! No getting all sentimental!

16:20.017 --> 16:23.297
Forgetting and being forgotten 
can both kiss my ass!

16:23.677 --> 16:26.507
Don't try to rank how painful things are!

16:26.977 --> 16:28.047
Subaru...

16:28.047 --> 16:30.307
And quit looking so discouraged!

16:30.817 --> 16:33.007
Did you forget, Julius?

16:33.007 --> 16:35.267
Wait, I mean, don't forget, Julius!

16:35.677 --> 16:37.977
My eyes know just how strong you are!

16:38.297 --> 16:39.937
My humiliation knows it!

16:40.487 --> 16:42.647
No matter who else may forget!

16:46.707 --> 16:47.657
Huh?

16:47.657 --> 16:51.117
Nothing. You truly are a remarkable man.

16:52.017 --> 16:54.177
Just realizing that all over again.

16:55.237 --> 16:57.677
I see. You're right.

16:58.427 --> 17:01.917
It's not as if I've been left 
behind by everything and everyone.

17:01.917 --> 17:03.967
I wouldn't say you were left behind.

17:03.967 --> 17:06.297
More like you're three lengths ahead.

17:06.847 --> 17:08.757
Is three enough to cover it?

17:08.757 --> 17:10.847
I oughta pound you!

17:10.847 --> 17:14.327
The pair Beako and I make is 
nothing like it was before!

17:25.137 --> 17:26.307
Ram.

17:26.307 --> 17:28.427
I was preparing for our departure.

17:28.427 --> 17:31.077
I changed her clothes and wiped her down.

17:32.427 --> 17:35.267
You're getting a lewd look 
on your face. Pervert.

17:35.267 --> 17:38.287
I kept quiet because I didn't know 
what to say, and that's what I get?

17:38.967 --> 17:40.787
You might die this time.

17:41.407 --> 17:42.977
Why are you doing this?

17:45.567 --> 17:50.767
I think... I just want to be the first 
thing she sees when she wakes up.

17:51.217 --> 17:53.547
Removing all emotions from it,

17:53.547 --> 17:56.227
I know it doesn't matter who wakes her up.

17:57.067 --> 17:58.187
But...

17:58.187 --> 18:00.667
when emotions come into play,

18:00.667 --> 18:02.727
I want to be the one to save her.

18:02.727 --> 18:05.867
I want to save her with all that I am.

18:08.947 --> 18:09.937
You're so dumb.

18:19.937 --> 18:22.477
Sorry it took me so long to see you.

18:22.477 --> 18:24.947
I had to take care of a 
bunch of other stuff...

18:26.327 --> 18:28.217
Sorry. That's just an excuse.

18:34.727 --> 18:37.677
It might finally get across.

18:39.007 --> 18:42.477
I'm going to get you back, Rem.

18:43.237 --> 18:46.257
That's my promise to you.

18:44.567 --> 18:48.067
<b>The Reason I'm Taking You With Me</b>

18:49.007 --> 18:54.487
I'm sorry I don't have anything prepared 
when you came all the way here.

18:54.487 --> 18:58.207
Oh, uh, sorry for
droppin' by without notice.

18:58.587 --> 19:01.037
We don't wanna put
you through any trouble.

19:01.547 --> 19:03.447
Oh, it's no trouble.

19:03.447 --> 19:08.987
The fact that you make the time 
to visit me is so reassuring.

19:11.987 --> 19:13.077
Hey—

19:11.987 --> 19:13.077
My husband...

19:14.277 --> 19:16.817
Garek will be home shortly.

19:16.817 --> 19:18.807
I have faith.

19:19.707 --> 19:21.767
When I was empty and had nothing,

19:22.507 --> 19:25.727
Garek gave me these past ten years.

19:26.337 --> 19:29.087
He even gave me an
 adorable son and daughter.

19:29.617 --> 19:33.487
So how could I not have faith in him?

19:35.167 --> 19:37.697
You're really strong.

19:37.697 --> 19:39.917
Yes, of course I am.

19:39.917 --> 19:43.397
I'm a mother of two, after all.

19:43.917 --> 19:45.597
I almost forgot!

19:45.597 --> 19:49.257
There's one thing
I wanted to ask you, too.

19:49.967 --> 19:56.007
Why do you show so much concern 
for us, Mister Gorgeous Tiger?

19:56.307 --> 20:02.587
I-I just... can't take my eyes 
off ya, for some reason...

20:03.187 --> 20:06.437
You guys are, well... 
kinda losin' it, aren't ya?

20:06.787 --> 20:08.257
Oh, how mean!

20:08.257 --> 20:11.457
But it's true, so I can't argue.

20:11.457 --> 20:14.657
Huh? Losing what? Hair?

20:14.657 --> 20:18.217
I lose a bunch of hair
when it gets hot, too!

20:24.357 --> 20:27.377
Are you all right, Mister Gorgeous Tiger?

20:28.107 --> 20:29.337
I'm not sure why,

20:29.857 --> 20:34.377
but you look like a child
who's about to cry.

20:40.807 --> 20:42.437
Mom...

20:43.727 --> 20:46.657
Mom... Mom...

20:46.657 --> 20:47.937
Mom!

20:48.497 --> 20:53.897
I... Mom, I...

20:57.127 --> 20:58.367
Garfiel.

20:59.827 --> 21:01.327
He's Garfiel.

21:06.727 --> 21:07.997
Garfiel.

21:09.127 --> 21:11.697
M-Mom...

21:12.527 --> 21:15.337
Mom!

21:20.727 --> 21:25.817
There, there, Garf. You're a good boy.

21:26.367 --> 21:28.517
You've been trying so hard all this time.

21:28.897 --> 21:35.117
I have! I tried so hard, went all-out...

21:35.117 --> 21:38.197
But I got so many things wrong...

21:38.507 --> 21:41.977
But still... But still, everyone...

21:44.327 --> 21:48.627
It's all right. It's all right, Garf.

21:49.327 --> 21:52.107
Your mother is with you now.

21:59.047 --> 22:01.437
Garf, you okee?

22:01.437 --> 22:02.507
Yeah.

22:02.887 --> 22:05.227
Are you all right, Gorgeous Tiger?

22:05.227 --> 22:08.137
A boy crying his eyes out? Unbelievable.

22:08.427 --> 22:11.177
Sorry to make ya worry like that.

22:11.177 --> 22:14.007
I'm gonna go now, so you can relax.

22:14.007 --> 22:16.237
Come visit again anytime.

22:16.697 --> 22:19.977
When you feel like crying, 
I'll lend you my shoulder

22:19.977 --> 22:21.987
in your mother's stead.

22:23.207 --> 22:26.077
I'll try to make sure that doesn't happen.

22:26.427 --> 22:30.037
Come on, now, you two. Say goodbye.

22:30.037 --> 22:32.827
See you next time, Gorgeous Tiger!

22:33.897 --> 22:35.957
Come on, Rafiel. You, too.

22:37.547 --> 22:39.427
Ra...fiel?

22:39.757 --> 22:41.867
Yes, Rafiel.

22:41.867 --> 22:45.287
Oh! Did I never introduce you to them?

22:46.087 --> 22:48.177
Their names are...

22:48.837 --> 22:51.147
Fred and Rafiel.

22:51.727 --> 22:54.357
I named them both.

22:54.647 --> 22:56.937
You... named them?

22:57.277 --> 22:58.017
Yes.

22:58.487 --> 23:01.467
When I was thinking of
cute names for babies,

23:01.467 --> 23:03.407
they just came to me.

23:03.757 --> 23:06.397
Fred and... Rafiel...

23:07.017 --> 23:10.047
Frederica... Garfiel...

23:15.127 --> 23:17.607
Well, see ya later, Rafiel and Fred!

23:17.607 --> 23:18.957
I'll come back!

23:18.957 --> 23:21.127
All right, Gorgeous Tiger!

23:21.537 --> 23:25.357
N-Next time, try not to cry, you hear?!

23:29.357 --> 23:32.267
Thanks, Mom.

23:34.087 --> 23:36.517
I'll come visit again!

23:36.517 --> 23:40.027
<b>Gorgeous Tiger Reloaded</b>

23:37.007 --> 23:39.077
Take care of yourselves till then!
